:INFO
Art. 21a Labelling of feedingstuffs for production animals
1 The indications laid down in Article 2 paragraph 2 may be used on processed animal feedingstuffs provided the following requirements are met:
a. The processed animal feedingstuff complies with the provisions of this Ordinance, in particular Articles 16a, 16kbis and 16l and their implementing provisions.
b. All ingredients of plant or animal origin contained in the processed animal feedingstuff consist of organic animal feed materials.
c. At least 95 per cent of the dry matter of the product consists of animal feed materials of organic origin.
2 In the case of processed animal feedingstuffs which do not comply with one of the requirements laid down in paragraph 1 letters b or c, only the indication ‘may be used in organic farming in accordance with the Organic Farming Ordinance’ may be used.
|

:NOTE
Art. 21a — Inserted by No I of the O of 26 Nov. 2003 (AS 2003 5347). Amended by No I of the O of 31 Oct. 2012, in force since 1 Jan. 2013 (AS 2012 6353).
Art. 21a — Amended by No I of the O of 6 Nov. 2024, in force since 1 Jan. 2025 (AS 2024 687).
|

:INFO
Art. 21b Further labelling requirements of feedingstuffs for production animals
The indications referred to in Article 21a must meet the following requirements:
they must not be more prominent than the description or name of the animal feedingstuff due to their colour, format or style of lettering;
with reference to the organic matter, they must indicate in the same field of vision the percentage of animal feedingstuffs which were produced on organic land and the percentage of animal feedingstuffs which were produced on land under conversion;
c. ...
d. they must give a list of the names of the animal feed materials produced organically or under conversion to organic farming.
|

:NOTE
Art. 21b — Inserted by No I of the O of 26 Nov. 2003, in force since 1 July 2004 (AS 2003 5347).
Art. 21b — Amended by No I of the O of 6 Nov. 2024, in force since 1 Jan. 2025 (AS 2024 687).
let. c — Repealed by No I of the O of 18 Nov. 2009, with effect from 1 Jan. 2010 (AS 2009 6317).
|

:INFO
Art. 21bbis Labelling of feedingstuffs for pets
1 The indications laid down in Article 2 paragraph 2 may be used in the product description and the details on the composition for processed feedingstuffs for pets provided that:
a. the feedingstuff meets the requirements laid down in Articles 16a paragraphs 2 and 7, 16kbis and 16l; and
b. at least 95 per cent by weight of the ingredients of agricultural origin were organically produced.
2 The indications laid down in Article 2 paragraph 2 may be used only in the details on the composition for processed feedingstuffs for pets provided that:
a. less than 95 per cent by weight of the ingredients of agricultural origin were organically produced;
b. only feed additives and processing aids permitted under Article 16a are used in the processing of the feedingstuff; and
c. the feedingstuff meets the requirements laid down in Articles 16a paragraphs 2 and 7, 16kbis and 16l.
|

:INFO
Art. 21bbis (continued)
3 The indications laid down in Article 2 paragraph 2 may be used in the details on the composition and in the same field of vision as the product description provided that:
a. the main ingredient is a game or fishing product;
b. all other ingredients of agricultural origin are purely organic; and
c. the feedingstuff meets the requirements laid down in Articles 16a paragraphs 2 and 7, 16kbis and 16l.
4 It must be stated in the details on the composition which animal feed materials are organically produced.
5 If an indication is used in accordance with paragraph 2 or 3, the reference to organic production may only be made in connection with the organic ingredients. The total percentage of organic ingredients in the ingredients of agricultural origin must be given in the details on the composition.
|

:INFO
Art. 21bbis (continued)
6 The indications and percentage information laid down in paragraph 5 must appear in the same colour and in the same size and style of lettering as the other information in the details on the composition.
|

:NOTE
Art. 21bbis — Inserted by No I of the O of 6 Nov. 2024, in force since 1 Jan. 2025 (AS 2024 687).
|

:INFO
Art. 21c Common labelling provisions
1 The code number of the certification body responsible for the operator who carried out the most recent production or processing operation must be given. The code number must meet the following requirements:
a. It must begin with the abbreviation for the country laid down in the international standard for two-letter country codes ISO 3166.
b. It must contain an indication referring to organic production.
c. It must contain a reference number issued by the Swiss accreditation body or by the competent authority in the case of products certified by bodies abroad.
2 FOAG may issue instructions regarding the format of code numbers.
|

:NOTE
Art. 21c — Inserted by No I of the O of 18 Nov. 2009, in force since 1 Jan. 2010 (AS 2009 6317).
Para. 2 — Inserted by No I of the O of 27 Oct. 2010, in force since 1 Jan. 2011 (AS 2010 5859).

